> Beginner questions:
> 
> What is the difference between MC and MR?

That's no beginner question :-)
MR is something necessary to have (obtained by specific items); deeper
down in the dungeons you won't survive long in the game without MR.
MC makes your life easier (depending on the grade of MC induced by
specific objects), since specific attacks won't succeed as easy.

> I haven't been able to 
> understand from reading about it in "Maniac's Ascension Guide".

In the game MR is a quite apparent conceivable concept, while MC is not.

> How do I feed a tripe ration to my pet?

Throw it to your pet or drop it on the floor; he will get it.

> Can I throw ANY object? When I want to (t)hrow something, the game only 
> promts me for "quiverable" weapons, but I want to chuck a potion.

Yes you can. Specify the inventory object letter when requested to specify
the object. If you want to see it in the menu then select * instead of ?.

> How do I find out my current base luck and/or item-added luck?

You won't. That's also some non-conceivable property. But you see some
of the luck increases ("four leaf clover"). If you carry luck stones
take care that they are always non-cursed!

> I have purchased all food items from a shop. Will it be restocked 
> ("closed for inventory")? If so, when?

No. In shops you'll get only what's been created when you entered the
level the first time. A closed shop will never open, you need some key
to open it, or use controlled teleport to get in (there are also other
means to get in). An open shop will never close if you haven't locked
the door yourself.

